course: dictionary
lesson: 10341
title: Transfer: moving from one place to another
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Transfer has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one fits. As a verb, it means to move someone or something from one place, person or group to another. «She transfers 5 marbles to her brother» means she gives them away, so she ends up with 5 fewer and he has 5 more.
explain: In sport, a footballer who moves to a new club has made a transfer. In science, heat transfers from a hot cup to the cold hands holding it. In each case, something moves from one place to another.
explain: Look at the words around transfer. «A bank transfer» means money sent from one account to another. A «transfer» you stick on a T-shirt is a picture you press onto it. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Transfer can be a verb (to transfer) or a noun (a transfer).
fact: «A transfer moves money between accounts; a standing order does it automatically, like £4 every Saturday, which is £16 over 4 Saturdays.»
fact: «Population transfer» means forcing people out of their homes and moving them elsewhere.
fact: Useful phrases: transfer to, transfer from, bank transfer, heat transfer.
fact: In UK English, a transfer can also be a picture you can stick or press onto something.
exercise: «She transfers 5 marbles to her brother.» Compared with before, how many marbles does she have now? | *5 fewer | The same number | 10 more | 5 more
exercise: In football, what does it mean when a player makes a transfer? | *A move from one club to another | A player who cannot run | A goal scored from a corner | A new pair of boots
exercise: «Heat transfers from hot to cold.» In this sentence, what does transfers mean? | *Moves from one place to another | Stops completely | Changes colour | Breaks into small pieces
test: «He made a bank transfer of £20 to his friend.» What does transfer mean here? | Painted a picture on the wall | Walked slowly across the room | Lost a game on purpose | *Sent money from one account to another
test: On a school trip, a UK friend says she has a transfer to stick on her T-shirt. What is it? | A bus ticket | *A picture you press onto the T-shirt | A type of heat | A move to a new school
exam: «Population transfer» means forcing people out of their homes and moving them elsewhere. What does population transfer mean? | *Forcing people out of their homes and moving them elsewhere | Painting houses in new colours | A party where everyone swaps seats | Counting how many people live in a town
